      "text": "To determine the number of distinct possible meals Crystal can buy, we need to consider all combinations of entrees, drinks, and desserts. Let's break it down step by step:\n\n1. **Identify the options for each category:**\n   - Entrees: Pizza, Chicken Teriyaki, Corn Dog, Fish and Chips\n   - Drinks: Lemonade, Root Beer\n   - Desserts: Frozen Yogurt, Chocolate Chip Cookie\n\n2. **Calculate the total number of combinations:**\n   - For each entree, Crystal can choose any of the 4 entrees.\n   - For each drink, she can choose any of the 2 drinks.\n   - For each dessert, she can choose any of the 2 desserts.\n\n   Therefore, the total number of distinct possible meals is given by the product of the number of choices in each category:\n   \\[\n   4 \\text{ (entrees)} \\times 2 \\text{ (drinks)} \\times 2 \\text{ (desserts)} = 4 \\times 2 \\times 2 = 16\n   \\]\n\n3. **List all possible combinations for verification:**\n   - Pizza with Lemonade, Frozen Yogurt, Chocolate Chip Cookie\n   - Pizza with Root Beer, Frozen Yogurt, Chocolate Chip Cookie\n   - Chicken Teriyaki with Lemonade, Frozen Yogurt, Chocolate Chip Cookie\n   - Chicken Teriyaki with Root Beer, Frozen Yogurt, Chocolate Chip Cookie\n   - Corn Dog with Lemonade, Frozen Yogurt, Chocolate Chip Cookie\n   - Corn Dog with Root Beer, Frozen Yogurt, Chocolate Chip Cookie\n   - Fish and Chips with Lemonade, Frozen Yogurt, Chocolate Chip Cookie\n   - Fish and Chips with Root Beer, Frozen Yogurt, Chocolate Chip Cookie\n\nThus, the total number of distinct possible meals Crystal can buy is \\(\\boxed{16}\\).",
